[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) said one bug, one fix queued. The reports merged into it held three problems,
and the queued parser fix closes only one of them. Each report is now merged into the ticket of its own
problem.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Each problem below has its own ticket. Shipping the parser fix will not stop the others.
</Callout>

## 1 · Shared parser reads day-first dates month first

[Ticket #1](https://github.com/kbuksakowski/mega-dev-support-desk/issues/1). Every tenant on file writes the
day first; the shared parser reads month first, so day and month swap. App, email and `booking-v2` form
reports. This is the bug #4471 described.

<CauseTable ticket={1} />

## 2 · booking-v3 form hints MM/DD/YYYY but reads the date day first

[Ticket #2](https://github.com/kbuksakowski/mega-dev-support-desk/issues/2). People type what the hint under
the date field tells them; the form reads it the tenant's way. A different code path: the parser fix will not
close it. In #4471 the desk's table marked these as having no ticket of their own.

<CauseTable ticket={2} />

## 3 · Invite date moves by one day

[Ticket #4](https://github.com/kbuksakowski/mega-dev-support-desk/issues/4). Day and month do not swap; the
date lands one day off, or differs by where the client is. The desk read these as a one-day move
(`desk-notes.json`) but filed them under the parser by tenant.

<CauseTable ticket={4} />

## How each report was placed

1. **Duplicates out first.** The ticket export pages overlap, so some reports come twice. One id, one report.
2. **By tenant, not by intake tag.** The tenant's locale and booking form decide the cause (`causes.ts`).
   Reports through a `booking-v3` form are the form hint; everything else is the shared parser.
3. **One-day moves on their own.** The reports the desk read as a one-day move did not swap day and month,
   so neither the parser nor the form hint explains them.

## Why it looked like one bug

- **Merged by subject.** [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on the subject line
  alone. "Wrong date" reads the same whatever caused it, so three problems landed in one ticket.
- **Intake tags are a guess.** Intake tags a report `hint` when the reporter's browser is `en-US` and
  `parser` otherwise. The browser is not the tenant, so the "tagged as" column disagrees with the cause.
- **The desk saw the one-day moves** after #4471 was marked known and noted them, but only as a footnote.

## What to change

- Ship the parser fix against #1. The form hint (#2) and the one-day move (#4) need their own fixes.
- Merge by cause, not by subject. Decision 0001 needs a new record; it is not edited.
- Before a big ticket is marked known, split it by cause and count once per problem.

